-- title:
--   Horizontal unramifiedness at a cusp over the X₀(M') floor, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a positive natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, assumed to satisfy $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$ for some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb` of `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ and the function field in question is generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral coefficients. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ (so $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$), and acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular $j$-function. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ after applying $A \to L$ coefficientwise. Consider the two-chart integral model $X =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`, glued from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$; let $z \in X$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y \in \operatorname{Spec}(A[j^{-1}]^{\mathrm{int}})$ be a point mapping to $z$ whose prime ideal is maximal, with $j^{-1} \in y$ and with every element of the pole chart whose image in $K$ is a non-unit of $W_0$ lying in $y$. Let $K_0$ be the analogous $L$-base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, with $K_0 \le K$, compatible $A$-algebra structures, and $j_0 \in K_0$ non-zero with the same Laurent expansion as $j$; let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the pole chart of $(A, K_0, j_0)$ to that of $(A, K, j)$ inducing the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$, used as the algebra structure. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}$ of the pole chart of $(A, K, j)$ with $\mathfrak{Q} \subseteq y$, of height $1$, and not containing the image of $\varpi$, the pole chart of $(A, K, j)$ is unramified at $\mathfrak{Q}$ over the pole chart of $(A, K_0, j_0)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ instance of the horizontal (characteristic-zero) half of the local analysis of the pole chart of $X_H(q^2M')$ over the $X_0(M')$ floor at a cusp lying on the branch cut out by $W_0$: the height-one primes below the special cusp $y$ that do not contain the uniformiser are unramified over the floor. It feeds the regularity statement for the fibre of the localised pole chart, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_two).
